(ROOT/'REVIEW.md').write_text('''The shared collector foundation is **blocked by six demonstrated issues in both frozen arms**. Candidate-v13.4 and baseline-v12.6-common-1 each retain 33 P / 5 F in the 38 new core cases, plus 3 P / 1 F in separate integration/diagnostic rows. The shared port audit passes. Raw total: 85 assertions, 73 P / 12 F; these are not native PFU scores.\n\nThe failures grant full coverage for an outside terminal frame with a true header, a capture reporting binding drift, an offscreen duplicate ID under another container, container-role witnesses, and unobserved off-axis width. A separate diagnosis failure replaces the original image root with the scanned production root. See [open issues](OPEN-ISSUES.md) and [structured review](review.json). All original failures remain sealed; none was dropped or regraded.\n\nOriginal-pixel RGB/alpha/full-width mismatch, root traversal, stale input, gap/terminal and common anchor negatives otherwise reject. Mocked collector export, review/evaluation, routing and independent pixel/receipt pins pass in both arms. Original source attachments and altered working copies remain retained.\n\nThe baseline source copy matches Git e75dd9227203dd06350a923cc249b79ff710687f. Its 13-path port is common coverage/root/indicator work; original resource, entry, retest/review-store and build/cache policy files/functions remain unchanged. Provider and both Swift runtime files match exactly across arms. Equivalent failures are still failures.\n\nThe old real iOS failed result remains byte-identical and was not read for fixture design or reinterpreted as P. No actual SDK/device/project, native UI, performance sample or business task ran here. The >=20% gate remains unevaluated and blocked.\n\n[SEAL.json](SEAL.json) binds the raw [artifact index](raw-artifact-index.json), source/fixture hashes, first failures, exact decisions and verified archive. Prior review-1 through review-4 remain unchanged.\n''')
(ROOT/'OPEN-ISSUES.md').write_text('''Six common blockers reproduce in both frozen arms. All evidence is HOST/SIMULATED; no product/native F is inferred.\n\n1. **SC01 terminal geometry:** set the last sentinel frame to y=500 outside y=0..96, keep the true containment header. Full/P still granted.\n2. **SC02 epoch error:** set original capture stable_binding=false. Pixel fallback still grants full/P.\n3. **SC03 duplicate identity:** add an offscreen duplicate leaf ID under a different container. Container lineage rescues its uniqueness.\n4. **SC04 fake leaf:** use container/ScrollView-role witness records with no listed children. They supply the required leaf anchors.\n5. **SC05 unobserved scope:** content width 128, observed viewport width 64. Strip-only proof becomes satisfied full_content/absence P despite broken closed-state premise.\n6. **SC06 image-root diagnosis:** diagnose the same valid strip with a nonempty production root. The source scan overwrites root and falsely marks full_content incomplete; an empty-source control remains complete.\n\nFor SC01–SC05, inspect `work/ARM/CASE/{observation,proof,coverage,evaluated}.json` using case names in `review.json`. SC06 has paired controls in `raw/ARM-diagnostic-root-result.json`. `first-failures` preserves both arms.\n\nNative/performance/business work remains closed. The original shared source was not modified.\n''')
